.TH MD_GET_WPM 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_wpm \- query the current channel Morse speed estimate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

double md_get_wpm(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query the current channel Morse speed estimate.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the current channel speed estimate in words per minute, or -1 for NULL
decoder or no current channel. This query has no errno-based failure return.
.SH REMARKS
Uses the PARIS timing convention and the channel's duration model. An estimate
may reflect initial priors before the model has learned the sender.
config.initial_wpm sets a prior, not a fixed receive speed or a guaranteed
decode range. md_get_channel() returns the corresponding estimate for each
channel.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3),
.BR md_config_init (3),
.BR md_get_state (3)
